# The order of the entries in wayfinder/decisions.md, which is generated.
#
# The order is curated, not numeric — the file opens 00, 03, 19, 01, 21, 08,
# grouping each decision beside the one it answers rather than beside the one
# that happened next. That curation is information, so it is recorded here
# rather than recomputed. It is NOT map.md's order either: of the 59 subjects
# with an entry, map.md indexes 50 under "Decisions so far", files eight under
# "Not yet specified" although their decision is written, and does not tag the
# walking skeleton at all. See ENG-327 and ENG-257.
#
# One key per entry, in the order they appear. A bare number is a ticket's
# first entry; `16:2` is its second. `skeleton` is the one entry whose subject
# is not a ticket — the walking skeleton, whose entry lives in the file it
# links to, compiler/README.md.
#
# Losing a line here silently drops an entry, which is how six of them went
# missing before stage 1. check-decisions.sh's NOENTRY is what catches that:
# it requires decisions.md to name every resolved ticket, and decisions.md is
# now this manifest's output.
